What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/sc2_vel_thrs
KernelVersion:	6.19
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		StealthChop2 velocity threshold in degrees per second. When the
		motor velocity is below this threshold, the driver uses
		StealthChop2 (voltage PWM) mode for quiet operation. Above this
		threshold, SpreadCycle mode is used. Writing 0 disables
		StealthChop2.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/cool_vel_thrs
KernelVersion:	6.19
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		CoolStep/StallGuard velocity threshold in degrees per second.
		StallGuard load measurement and CoolStep current regulation are
		only active when the motor velocity is above this threshold.
		Writing 0 disables CoolStep and StallGuard.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/fullstep_vel_thrs
KernelVersion:	6.19
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Fullstep velocity threshold in degrees per second. When the motor
		velocity exceeds this threshold, the driver switches to fullstep
		operation for maximum torque at high velocities. Writing 0
		disables automatic fullstep switching.
